{"title":"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangle with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in an equilateral triangle. Another rectangle with height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is also inscribed in the triangle. The base of the second rectangle can be written as a fully simplified fraction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40ef7c2ccddab492a260f3d0a444a9d907816219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+b\\sqrt{3}}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"43\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/7/b977623001c7231965610580b12895977c8cefdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$gcd(a,b,c)=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Sprint13.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/77/Sprint13.jpg/400px-Sprint13.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"318\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/77/Sprint13.jpg/600px-Sprint13.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/7/77/Sprint13.jpg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Accuracy12sol.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/cb/Accuracy12sol.jpeg/500px-Accuracy12sol.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"400\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/cb/Accuracy12sol.jpeg/750px-Accuracy12sol.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/c/cb/Accuracy12sol.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>We are given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/b/e4b7ed187ff32a41734b0d9079e1007de7536ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, from which in rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c7c07090dde22654e05ef42ac932e18d9869d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFDA$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> we can conclude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/24096979a27c72ccde79e7e4889bf4e4be7a632b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d5204a6910d20a4ff2968ad55671e3cfa350e9da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=2$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc83ad61217b1d406190a33eaba97c732052e179.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB-AE=2-1=1=BE.\\]\" width=\"233\" height=\"13\" /> \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7851904e7bde074abb4080c9d00cd9277af793.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C =60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e89721381056cdba25ac52de41958bb69a49aef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BFE = 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" /> by corresponding angles. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a97e1a68fb2e86b2a14d9c9d523154d6a80794f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEF = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" /> and it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f00afb3996c4aa5426ec79a3d7334010023053d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BFE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> right triangle. \n</p><p>Since the side opposite the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> angle in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f00afb3996c4aa5426ec79a3d7334010023053d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BFE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we use our <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> ratios to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/5/e5562329d3e446a1313f3e8f03d658e4e271a4b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"141\" height=\"48\" /> In rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c7c07090dde22654e05ef42ac932e18d9869d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFDA$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />, we also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/5168f3bbd1871b44d9706218733e4e8208903699.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AD=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\]\" width=\"84\" height=\"41\" /> Analogously, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/5/ae5e789418fb4a8addaedb388dc7c4defae800fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[QP=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\]\" width=\"84\" height=\"41\" /> Since we are looking for the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the horizontal rectangle and we are given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fda99c678c89fc5078e0c093a72a55cccae62e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PA=1,\\]\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/1/7016fab02a1a984e24bc1ffb6eb25d98a264d779.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d=QP+PA+AD=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}+1+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}=\\frac{3+2\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\]\" width=\"394\" height=\"41\" /> This gives us an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/038d14d687d66b7e418327511018ecb4530018d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+3+3=\\boxed{8}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" /> ~ samrocksnature\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the angles of an equilateral triangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae82fc01ad7a31ae4c8a590a57a1fc4f150d228.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^o$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" />, we have by similar triangles that the length of the segments of the \"small\" rectangles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/c/e5cb6e7c42d6bf0c332b448f0d28fff6c0aaaef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />, meaning the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/525ddf0e954497d1ea4f89d699e0f423ad443f76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3+2\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\implies 3+2+3=\\boxed{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"236\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f40b1e5cfdb4e4b37d0f5d1c57a5c893020e39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\linebreak$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"22\" />\n~Geometry285\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems\">Other 2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Answer Key\">2021 JMPSC Accuracy Answer Key</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JMPSC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"JMPSC Problems and Solutions\">All JMPSC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ol>\n<p>The problems on this page are copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jmpsc.org\">Junior Mathematicians' Problem Solving Competition</a>. <span class=\"mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:JMPSC.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/120px-JMPSC.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/180px-JMPSC.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ab/JMPSC.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018015828\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.069 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 186/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 183/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5976/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.572      1 Template:JMPSC_Notice\n100.00%    5.572      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21593:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018015828 and revision id 158073. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}